### ScholarHub REST API - works in VS Code (REST Client extension) and Visual Studio 2022.
### Change the port to the one shown when you run "dotnet run".
@host = https://localhost:5001

### 1) Get a JWT token
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@scholarhub.local", "password": "Admin@12345" }

### 2) Paste the token below, then try the requests
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

GET {{host}}/api/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/students?q=&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/students
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentCode": "BCA001", "fullName": "Asha Patil", "dateOfBirth": "2005-04-12",
  "gender": "Female", "email": "asha@example.com", "phone": "9876543210",
  "address": "Pune", "departmentId": 1, "courseId": 1, "semester": 1,
  "admissionDate": "2026-07-01", "isActive": true
}

###
GET {{host}}/api/results/student/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
